{"duration_api_ms":10366,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3400ddb1-c9f7-4f28-9493-d9d4bd0e060e","total_cost_usd":0.0012963,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":722,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1804,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1460},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":722,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1804,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":722,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":722},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1264,"outputTokens":2051,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":722,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0012963,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1682,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":722,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Start with the fund's website.** Rule 6c-11 requires ETFs to post their full portfolio holdings daily before market open, usually under a \"Holdings\" tab. These are the holdings used for that day's NAV. For lagged detail, check the fund's N-PORT filings on SEC EDGAR, and read the prospectus and SAI for basket policies.\n\n**Holdings vs. transaction basket:** Holdings show what the fund owns. The transaction basket, or PCF (Portfolio Composition File), lists the securities and cash used in creations and redemptions. It can differ through cash-in-lieu, substitutions, or custom baskets. It is distributed through NSCC to authorized participants, so don't assume it's public.\n\n**Requesting the PCF:**\n- Ask your broker, who may be an AP or can route the request through one.\n- Contact the sponsor's client services or distributor and ask whether the current basket file is available to non-APs.\n- Check whether the sponsor's site publishes a creation/redemption basket link. Some do, but not all.","ttft_ms":7682,"type":"result","duration_ms":9013,"uuid":"e3793bab-e90d-481b-a7f5-2bebcfb4ad78","ttft_stream_ms":488,"time_to_request_ms":70,"first_content_frame_ms":488,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
